// transfer_single -- operation model §3.2, group 1, level: end-to-end.
// (`run_transfer` in the first pass; renamed for symmetry with transfer_list.)
//
// completes_when: the channel's DONE (or ERR) interrupt has been observed and
//                 the CHn_CSR read has returned the status and cleared the
//                 source.
// waits for:      channel DONE or ERR, on the per-channel interrupt. This is
//                 the core driver FSM: submit -> RUNNING -> completion.
//
// The whole transfer: program, arm, wait, report. This is the operation every
// downstream consumer actually calls, and in SOFTWARE mode it needs nothing
// but memory access plus a completion wait -- which is why the model retargets
// to firmware and post-silicon nearly for free.
//
// TWO CALLERS' OBLIGATIONS THIS SIGNATURE DOES NOT ENCODE:
//
//   mode == HW_HANDSHAKE: this call cannot complete on its own. Something must
//   be calling request_chunk() on the matching wb_dma_hs_c concurrently. A
//   handshake transfer is inherently a parallel composition of one MMIO
//   operation and N handshake operations (§2.2).
//
//   cfg.auto_restart: this call is DELIBERATELY NON-TERMINATING. CSR bit 11
//   sets DONE only once ARS is clear, so the completion event exists but
//   nothing in this operation causes it. Another thread must clear ARS
//   (set_auto_restart(0)) or abort the channel (stop_channel()); the in-flight
//   iteration then retires and DONE asserts. It is a blocking read on a stream
//   that ends when someone closes it -- so an ARS transfer must never be the
//   only operation a scenario waits on.
import wb_dma_regs_pkg::*;
import wb_dma_types_pkg::*;

extend component wb_dma_ch_ops_c {

    target function wb_dma_status_e transfer_single(wb_dma_ch_cfg_s cfg) {
        wb_dma_ch_csr_s csr;

        configure_channel(cfg);

        // Arm. Read-modify-write so the configuration just written survives;
        // the read also clears the ROC status bits, which is harmless here
        // because the channel has not started yet.
        csr = regs.csr.read();
        csr.ch_en = 1;
        regs.csr.write(csr);

        return wait_completion();
    }
}
